# Gemini Agent Hub

**An enterprise multi-agent assistant built on Google's Agent Development Kit (ADK) and Gemini. It has hybrid RAG with citations, multimodal document ingestion, Workspace-style tool connectors, governance guardrails, and a one-command deploy to Cloud Run.**

![ci](https://github.com/guru-prasath-j/gemini-agent-hub/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)

Gemini Agent Hub is a reference implementation of the pattern enterprises follow when they adopt generative AI internally. A coordinator agent routes each request to specialist agents. Those agents ground their answers in company documents and act on business systems through tools. Every turn passes through PII redaction, prompt-injection screening, role-based tool access and an audit trail that lands in BigQuery.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    U[User / Web UI] -->|HTTPS, IAM / IAP| R[Cloud Run · FastAPI]
    R --> RN[ADK Runner + Session Service]
    RN --> C{{concierge<br/>coordinator agent}}
    C -->|transfer_to_agent| K[knowledge_agent]
    C -->|transfer_to_agent| W[workspace_agent]
    K --> T1[search_knowledge_base]
    T1 --> IDX[(Hybrid index<br/>Gemini embeddings + BM25<br/>RRF fusion · MMR)]
    W --> T2[calendar · free slots · tickets · directory]
    T2 --> GC[Google Calendar API / demo backend]
    subgraph Guardrails [ADK callbacks on every agent]
      G1[PII redaction] --- G2[Prompt-injection screen] --- G3[Tool RBAC] --- G4[Audit log]
    end
    C -.-> Guardrails
    K -.-> Guardrails
    W -.-> Guardrails
    ING[/v1/documents<br/>txt · md · PDF · images/] -->|Gemini multimodal extraction| IDX
    G4 -->|Cloud Logging sink| BQ[(BigQuery audit dataset)]
    RN --> G[Gemini 2.5 Flash<br/>Vertex AI or Gemini API]
```

## What it demonstrates

| Capability | Where |
|---|---|
| **Multi-agent orchestration with ADK.** A coordinator plus specialists, routed with `transfer_to_agent`, with shared callbacks across agents | `app/agents/root.py` |
| **RAG with citations.** Structure-aware chunking, Gemini embeddings with retrieval task types, BM25 fused by Reciprocal Rank Fusion, and MMR diversification | `app/rag/` |
| **Multimodal ingestion.** Scanned PDFs, screenshots and forms are transcribed by Gemini into markdown, then indexed | `app/rag/ingest.py` |
| **Connecting LLMs to enterprise tools.** A Google Calendar connector over ADC, plus ticketing and directory tools behind a backend protocol | `app/tools/workspace.py` |
| **Security and governance.** PII redaction before the model and the logs, direct and *indirect* (document-borne) prompt-injection defence, role-based tool allowlists, and structured audit events | `app/governance/` |
| **Serverless deployment.** Container on Cloud Run, Cloud Build pipeline, and Terraform for Artifact Registry, a least-privilege service account, a private service and a BigQuery audit sink | `Dockerfile`, `deploy/`, `infra/terraform/` |
| **Evaluation as a quality gate.** A golden set with recall@k and MRR in CI, plus a live mode that checks answer facts, citations and p50/p95 latency | `evals/` |
| **Deterministic tests.** A scripted fake LLM drives the real ADK Runner end to end (routing, tools, RBAC, injection blocking, SSE streaming), with no API key needed | `tests/` |

## Quickstart

```bash
git clone https://github.com/guru-prasath-j/gemini-agent-hub && cd gemini-agent-hub
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev,workspace]"
cp .env.example .env            # add a free Gemini API key from aistudio.google.com
set -a; source .env; set +a

make test                       # 23 tests, fully offline
make eval                       # retrieval quality gate
make run                        # http://localhost:8080 (chat UI + API)
make dev                        # ADK dev UI with event traces at http://localhost:8000
```

To run with no credentials at all, set `EMBEDDER=hashing`. Retrieval, guardrails and tests all work offline. Only the chat turns need Gemini.

### Try it

```bash
curl -s localhost:8080/v1/chat -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"message":"How do I roll back a bad Cloud Run release?","role":"employee"}' | jq

# guests can read docs but cannot act
curl -s localhost:8080/v1/chat -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"message":"My laptop was stolen, open a P1 ticket","role":"guest"}' | jq .reply

# add a scanned PDF or a screenshot to the knowledge base (admin)
curl -s localhost:8080/v1/documents -H 'x-user-role: admin' -F file=@policy-scan.pdf | jq
```

`data/sample_docs/vendor-faq.md` contains a planted instruction ("Ignore all previous instructions…"). Ask about vendor onboarding and you'll see that passage quarantined in the audit log instead of reaching the model.

## Deploy to Google Cloud

```bash
export PROJECT_ID=my-project REGION=asia-south1
gcloud config set project $PROJECT_ID

# 1. infrastructure: APIs, Artifact Registry, runtime SA, BigQuery audit sink
cd infra/terraform
terraform init
terraform apply -var project_id=$PROJECT_ID \
  -var image=$REGION-docker.pkg.dev/$PROJECT_ID/agent-hub/gemini-agent-hub:bootstrap
cd ../..

# 2. test, build, push, deploy (Cloud Build)
make deploy
```

The service is deployed **private** (`--no-allow-unauthenticated`). Grant `roles/run.invoker` to a group, or put it behind IAP and derive the role from the verified identity rather than the request body. On Vertex AI, the runtime service account only holds `aiplatform.user`, plus log, metric and trace writers. No API keys are stored.

## Design notes

- **Why hybrid retrieval?** Policy questions mix exact tokens ("SEV1", "asia-south1", "INR 25,000") with paraphrase. BM25 catches the tokens, embeddings catch the meaning, and RRF merges the two without having to tune score scales.
- **Why guardrails in callbacks?** `before_model_callback`, `before_tool_callback` and `after_tool_callback` run for *every* agent. A new specialist added later inherits redaction, RBAC and auditing automatically.
- **Indirect injection.** Retrieved passages are screened before they're returned to the model, and the knowledge agent is told that passages are data, not instructions.
- **Swappable backends.** The index API mirrors Vertex AI Vector Search and AlloyDB pgvector, sessions switch to Cloud SQL via `SESSION_DB_URL` (ADK `DatabaseSessionService`), and the calendar switches to Google with `WORKSPACE_BACKEND=google`.

## Roadmap

- Vertex AI Vector Search backend and a Cloud Run Job for re-indexing from GCS
- Model Armor and Sensitive Data Protection in place of the regex layers
- A2A endpoint so other agents can call the hub
- OpenTelemetry traces to Cloud Trace

